WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:04.847
Turn any document into Markdown for notes and AI chats.

2
00:00:06.347 --> 00:00:12.536
Why Markdown is worth it, how PDF, Word, PowerPoint, Excel, email and notebooks

3
00:00:12.536 --> 00:00:18.569
are read in the browser, and how to deal with saved web pages and old Windows

4
00:00:18.569 --> 00:00:19.275
drawings.

5
00:00:20.675 --> 00:00:23.070
Why Markdown is worth the trouble.

6
00:00:23.070 --> 00:00:28.141
A Markdown file is plain text with a few marks for structure: a hash for

7
00:00:28.141 --> 00:00:31.875
a heading, a dash for a list item, pipes for a table.

8
00:00:33.175 --> 00:00:37.569
How each kind of file is read. Every format needs its own reader.

9
00:00:38.869 --> 00:00:44.101
Notebooks without Jupyter. A Jupyter notebook is JSON with code, text and

10
00:00:44.101 --> 00:00:46.251
the outputs from the last run.

11
00:00:47.551 --> 00:00:52.672
Privacy. Documents are often the most private files we have: contracts,

12
00:00:52.672 --> 00:00:54.548
payslips, medical letters.

13
00:00:55.848 --> 00:00:59.397
To try it, open Anything to Markdown in OpenFile.

14
00:00:59.397 --> 00:01:03.525
Drop in a file, adjust the settings and press the button.

15
00:01:03.525 --> 00:01:07.219
It all runs on your device, so nothing is uploaded.

16
00:01:08.948 --> 00:01:13.236
Read the full post, with live demos, on the OpenFile blog.
